================================================================================
Binary releases (pre-built downloads) — what they embed
================================================================================

The statements above describe this SOURCE REPOSITORY. Pre-built binaries may also
be published for convenience (e.g. on the project's releases page). Being
compiled, a binary necessarily EMBEDS a portion of game-derived data that the
build bakes in — it cannot be reconstructed at runtime the way the source tree
regenerates it. Concretely, a release binary contains:

  * the executable's static data segment (game tables and some encoded UI text),
    reconstructed from SLUS_004.47;
  * a small PS1 BIOS-derived kanji glyph set used by the text renderer;
  * the reconstructed text/pointer tables and functional game-data tables.

This is game-derived data (© Konami) and BIOS-derived data (© Sony), embedded so
the port can run; no ownership is claimed over any of it. It is only a FRACTION
of the game — the bulk of the content (dialogue, maps, event scripts, audio, and
video) is NOT included and is read at runtime from the disc image you supply. A
release binary is non-functional without your own legally-owned copy of the game.
If the copyright holder objects to this, binaries will be withdrawn on request.
